# Skill: github-mapping (PATTERN §17, v2.10)

> Adapter Cursor della skill `github-mapping` definita in `.claude/skills/github-mapping.md`.
> Costrutto: Cursor rule `.mdc`. File equivalente Claude Code: `.claude/skills/github-mapping.md`.

Mapping provider-specific GitHub. Invocata da `publisher-protocol` Fase 4.

## Auth check (Fase 1 di publisher-protocol)

```bash
gh auth status
gh repo view <target> --json viewerPermission
```

`viewerPermission` richiesto: `ADMIN | MAINTAIN | WRITE`. Altrimenti WARNING.

## Mapping artefatti

### Epica (default `epic_to: milestone`)

**GitHub Milestone**: `EP-XXX: <title>`, descrizione = body markdown (troncato 10k).
Stato: `open` se in-progress/todo; `closed` se done.

Alternativa `epic_to: issue-label`: Issue con label `kanban:epic`.

### User Story (default `story_to: issue-label`)

**GitHub Issue**: `US-YYY: <title>`, body markdown.
Label: `kanban:story` + `role:<role>` + `priority:<level>`.
Milestone: epica genitore.

### Task (default `task_to: issue-label`)

**GitHub Issue**: `TSK-ZZZ: <title>`, body markdown.
Label: `kanban:task` + `layer:<layer>` + `consumer:<consumer>` + `priority:<level>` + `estimate:<n>`.

### Sprint (default `sprint_to: milestone`)

**GitHub Milestone**: `Sprint NN`, descrizione = sezione sprint.

## Body template

Ogni artefatto include:
1. **Header blockquote**: metadati Factory (layer, consumer, priority, estimate, citazione)
2. **Body verbatim** del file locale
3. **Footer**: mirror push-only + source-of-truth reference

Wikilink `[[slug]]` → lasciati testuali + nota HTML comment.

## Comandi gh CLI

### CREATE — Epica come Milestone

```bash
gh api repos/<target>/milestones --method POST \
   --field title="EP-XXX: <title>" \
   --field description="$(cat /tmp/factory-publish-EP-XXX.md)" \
   --field state="open"
# → external_id: github:milestone-<num>
```

### CREATE — Story/Task come Issue

```bash
gh issue create --repo <target> \
   --title "US-YYY: <title>" \
   --body-file /tmp/factory-publish-US-YYY.md \
   --label "kanban:story,role:cittadino,priority:high" \
   --milestone "<milestone-title>"
# → external_id: github:<num>
```

### UPDATE

```bash
gh issue edit <num> --repo <target> --body-file /tmp/... --add-label "..." --remove-label "..."
gh api repos/<target>/milestones/<num> --method PATCH --field state="open|closed"
```

### State sync (done → close)

```bash
gh issue close <num> --repo <target> --reason completed
```

## Pre-flight labels

Prima della prima Fase 4:
```bash
gh label create "kanban:epic" --color "B60205" --force
gh label create "kanban:story" --color "0E8A16" --force
gh label create "kanban:task" --color "1D76DB" --force
gh label create "layer:be" --color "5319E7" --force
# ... (layer:fe, layer:db, layer:qa, layer:infra)
```

## Rate limit e sicurezza

- Rate limit: 5000 req/h; sleep 1s tra operazioni.
- Token (`GH_TOKEN`) mai loggato. Body files `/tmp/factory-publish-*.md` cancellati dopo Fase 4.
- Scope token minimo: `repo:issues:write` + `repo:metadata:read`.

## Limitazioni Cursor

- **Terminal**: tutti i comandi `gh` via terminal integrato.
- **Body files**: crea file temporanei in `/tmp/factory-publish-*.md` con Write, poi usa nel comando.
- **Rate limit**: aggiungi `sleep 1` nel terminal tra operazioni consecutive.
